ammalian metabolite produced during a metabolic reaction in a mouse (<em>Mus musculus</em>).","id":75771,"biological_role":true},{"application":false,"chemical_role":false,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:23357","name":"cofactor","definition":"An organic molecule or ion (usually a metal ion) that is required by an enzyme for its activity. It may be attached either loosely (coenzyme) or tightly (prosthetic group).","id":23357,"biological_role":true},{"application":false,"chemical_role":false,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:76971","name":"Escherichia coli metabolite","definition":"Any bacterial metabolite produced during a metabolic reaction in <em>Escherichia coli</em>.","id":76971,"biological_role":true},{"application":false,"chemical_role":false,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:75772","name":"Saccharomyces cerevisiae metabolite","definition":"Any  fungal metabolite produced during a metabolic reaction in Baker's yeast (<em>Saccharomyces cerevisiae </em>).","id":75772,"biological_role":true},{"application":true,"chemical_role":false,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:50733","name":"nutraceutical","definition":"A product in capsule, tablet or liquid form that provide essential nutrients, such as a vitamin, an essential mineral, a protein, an herb, or similar nutritional substance.","id":50733,"biological_role":false},{"application":false,"chemical_role":false,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:27314","name":"water-soluble vitamin (role)","definition":"Any vitamin that dissolves in water and readily absorbed into tissues for immediate use. Unlike the fat-soluble vitamins, they are not stored in the body and need to be replenished regularly in the diet and will rarely accumulate to toxic levels since they are quickly excreted from the body via urine.","id":27314,"biological_role":true}],"is_released":true}